60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the cheapest per head, but the eight-to-a-room density is a liability.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A removes the cooking duty entirely. That is a significant reduction in organizer workload.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A is the only one where we are all in one building. That is essential for mixing.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option A offers a private building. That means we control the noise levels.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A has a fixed fee. No hidden costs, no lottery risk. It is the safest.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the fixed fee for A is higher than C, but it avoids the deficit risk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, yes. The cost of A is the cost of not having to cook or clean.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, and the cost of A is the cost of actually talking to each other.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, and the cost of A is the cost of sleeping well. I have seen the hall schedule.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the flat fee for A means no one pays more for their own comfort.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is free for the hall, but the accommodation costs for commuters are unpredictable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Option B means we are on campus. That means we are on duty. I reject it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,Option B means we are scattered. That means we do not mix. I reject it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,Option B means we are in the hall. That means we are in the noise. I reject it.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Option B means the costs are variable. That means the burden is uneven. I reject it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is risky. Option B is chaotic. Option A is stable.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Option A is the only one that protects the organizers from burnout.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,Option A is the only one that protects the club from disintegration.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Option A is the only one that protects the members from exhaustion.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Option A is the only one that protects the members from inequity.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
